{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":183,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Then Job answered,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":543},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":184,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“Truly I know that it is so, but how can man be just with God?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":545},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":185,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"If he is pleased to contend with him, he can’t answer him one time in a thousand.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":548},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":186,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"God is wise in heart, and mighty in strength. Who has hardened himself against him and prospered?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":551},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":187,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"He removes the mountains, and they don’t know it, when he overturns them in his anger.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":554},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":188,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"He shakes the earth out of its place. Its pillars tremble.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":557},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":189,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"He commands the sun and it doesn’t rise, and seals up the stars.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":560},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":190,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"He alone stretches out the heavens, and treads on the waves of the sea.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":563},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":191,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"He makes the Bear, Orion, and the Pleiades, and the rooms of the south.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":566},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":192,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"He does great things past finding out; yes, marvelous things without number.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":569},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":193,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"Behold, he goes by me, and I don’t see him. He passes on also, but I don’t perceive him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":572},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":194,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"Behold, he snatches away. Who can hinder him? Who will ask him, ‘What are you doing?’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":575},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":195,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"“God will not withdraw his anger. The helpers of Rahab stoop under him.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":580},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":196,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"How much less will I answer him, and choose my words to argue with him?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":583},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":197,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"Though I were righteous, yet I wouldn’t answer him. I would make supplication to my judge.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":586},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":198,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"If I had called, and he had answered me, yet I wouldn’t believe that he listened to my voice.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":589},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":199,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"For he breaks me with a storm, and multiplies my wounds without cause.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":592},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":200,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"He will not allow me to catch my breath, but fills me with bitterness.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":595},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":201,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"If it is a matter of strength, behold, he is mighty! If of justice, ‘Who,’ says he, ‘will summon me?’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":598},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":202,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"Though I am righteous, my own mouth will condemn me. Though I am blameless, it will prove me perverse.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":601},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":203,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"I am blameless. I don’t respect myself. I despise my life.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":604},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":204,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"“It is all the same. Therefore I say he destroys the blameless and the wicked.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":609},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":205,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"If the scourge kills suddenly, he will mock at the trial of the innocent.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":612},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":206,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"The earth is given into the hand of the wicked. He covers the faces of its judges. If not he, then who is it?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":615},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":207,"verse_start":25,"verse_end":25,"verse_label":"25","text":"“Now my days are swifter than a runner. They flee away. They see no good.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":620},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":208,"verse_start":26,"verse_end":26,"verse_label":"26","text":"They have passed away as the swift ships, as the eagle that swoops on the prey.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":623},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":209,"verse_start":27,"verse_end":27,"verse_label":"27","text":"If I say, ‘I will forget my complaint, I will put off my sad face, and cheer up,’","is_omitted":0,"source_line":626},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":210,"verse_start":28,"verse_end":28,"verse_label":"28","text":"I am afraid of all my sorrows. I know that you will not hold me innocent.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":629},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":211,"verse_start":29,"verse_end":29,"verse_label":"29","text":"I will be condemned. Why then do I labor in vain?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":632},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":212,"verse_start":30,"verse_end":30,"verse_label":"30","text":"If I wash myself with snow, and cleanse my hands with lye,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":635},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":213,"verse_start":31,"verse_end":31,"verse_label":"31","text":"yet you will plunge me in the ditch. My own clothes will abhor me.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":638},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":214,"verse_start":32,"verse_end":32,"verse_label":"32","text":"For he is not a man, as I am, that I should answer him, that we should come together in judgment.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":641},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":215,"verse_start":33,"verse_end":33,"verse_label":"33","text":"There is no umpire between us, that might lay his hand on us both.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":644},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":216,"verse_start":34,"verse_end":34,"verse_label":"34","text":"Let him take his rod away from me. Let his terror not make me afraid;","is_omitted":0,"source_line":647},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":9,"verse_ordinal":217,"verse_start":35,"verse_end":35,"verse_label":"35","text":"then I would speak, and not fear him, for I am not so in myself.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":650}]}